		summary = "The **hoatzin** (**Opisthocomus hoazin**) is a species of tropical [[Bird|bird]] found in swamps, riparian forests, and [[Mangrove|mangroves]] of the Amazon and Orinoco Basins in South America. It is the only extant species in the genus **Opisthocomus** which is the only extant genus in the family Opisthocomidae under the order Opisthocomiformes. Despite being the subject of intense debate by specialists, the [[Taxonomy (biology)|taxonomic]] position of this family is still far from clear.",
