		aliases = { "Hornbills", "Bucerotidae" },
		summary = "**Hornbills** are [[Bird|birds]] found in tropical and subtropical Africa, Asia and [[Melanesia]] of the family **Bucerotidae**. They are characterized by a long, down-curved bill which is frequently brightly coloured and sometimes has a horny casque on the upper mandible. Hornbills have a two-lobed kidney. They are the only birds in which the first and second neck vertebrae (the atlas and axis respectively) are fused together; this probably provides a more stable platform for carrying the bill. The family is omnivorous, feeding on fruit and small animals. They are monogamous breeders nesting in natural cavities in trees and sometimes cliffs.",
