		summary = "**Pterosaurs** are an extinct clade of warm-blooded flying reptiles in the order **Pterosauria**. They existed during most of the [[Mesozoic]]: from the Late Triassic to the end of the [[Cretaceous]] (228 million to 66 million years ago). Pterosaurs are the earliest [[Vertebrate|vertebrates]] known to have evolved powered flight. Their wings were formed by a membrane of skin, muscle, and other [[Tissue (biology)|tissues]] stretching from the ankles to a dramatically lengthened fourth finger.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
